From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: wrap the position of a full ring to 0"

This reverts commit 222d04cf55bc (stable 833cfd0e4a7b in 7.3.4).

The q6asm DSP returns a playback buffer as soon as it has copied it,
not once it has played it. Right after a start it takes every queued
period at once, so the position reaches appl_ptr before the
application has built up any lead, and with the position no longer
one frame short ALSA calls that an underrun. On a Mangmi Pocket Max
(SM8250, PipeWire) every stream underruns ~150 ms after it starts,
each time the sink wakes from idle: stop, prepare, start, ~25 ms of
silence. Without the queue reset at prepare, the recovery never plays
again at all.

The one-frame-short position kept that underrun hidden through 7.3.3.
Go back to it until the position comes from what the DSP has
rendered rather than from the buffers it has returned.

Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index ca582eb..ebf6bb1 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -487,10 +487,11 @@ static snd_pcm_uframes_t q6asm_dai_pointer(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	struct q6asm_dai_rtd *prtd = runtime->private_data;
 	snd_pcm_uframes_t ptr;
 
-	/* a full lap of period buffers is the start of the ring again */
-	ptr = q6asm_get_hw_pointer(prtd->audio_client, substream->stream) % runtime->periods;
+	ptr = q6asm_get_hw_pointer(prtd->audio_client, substream->stream) * runtime->period_size;
+	if (ptr)
+		return ptr - 1;
 
-	return ptr * runtime->period_size;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int q6asm_dai_hw_params(struct snd_soc_component *component,
